      "description": "- Working on redesigning existing websites to be more author friendly. Leveraging Adobe Experience Manager to make it easier for 3rd party vendors post content such as articles, photos, and videos. Recently helped launch a redesign to TheBlock.com, a content site focusing on Chevrolet Performance events.\n\n- Provided aid to a team that was making changes to an existing inventory system for used and pre-owned vehicles to better comply with government regulations.\n\n- Was part of the team working on a customer facing website (shopcarsnow.com) to help facilitate the buying of new and used cars online.\n\n- Worked on a web application that was used to help give customers, using a soft credit check, a rough estimate on the monthly payment they can afford. This estimate was then used to help the customer find vehicles in their area that was under this monthly payment.\n\n- Worked on a South African customer facing website for used vehicles. Primarily worked on the back-end, using C# and .NET, where data was pulled from a 3rd party API, processed, and stored in an SQL database. To speed up the batch import parallel programming was used.",
